#
# The cycles one emulated run takes (mockingbird_rules.h MR3), in Sutra:
# steps of cost cycles each, and stall cycles besides. steps fits 9(9),
# cost 9(4) and stall 9(9), so a larger or a negative one is a size error:
# refused, never cut short. cycles.tb says the same in Trebago, which
# answers up to 64 bits: past these pictures the two disagree and the run
# is held.
record run-cycles
  steps: 9(9)
  cost: 9(4)
  stall: 9(9)
  cycles: 9(14)
procedure
  compute cycles = steps * cost + stall
  answer cycles
